# chromium - web browser (Wayland only: no X11, GTK or Qt; accessibility through at-spi2-core).
# Optional, off by default.
# Google's official source release (chromium-browser-official; unsigned: a checksum file on the
# same host, which the pin matches). musl patches from Alpine Linux (aports, pinned commit
# 7628bce8) and copium (157.1), refreshed to apply exactly (BusyBox patch has no fuzz):
# files/patches, applied in the order of files/patches/series; musl-pwritev2 is cig's own: musl
# 1.2.6's pwrite() calls pwritev2, so every sandbox policy that allows pwrite64 allows it too
# (the GPU process was killed by its seccomp filter). Prebuilt binaries in the source
# tree are deleted; Chromium's own copies of its libraries are used (ffmpeg, ICU, harfbuzz...),
# except fontconfig and libffi (its bundled fontconfig is configured for glibc).
# Crubit (Rust <-> C++ bindings, needed by Chromium's Rust parts) and gnrt (Chromium's Rust build
# file generator) are built from source with cargo, offline, from the crates their Cargo.lock
# files name (each pin matches the lock file's checksum).
# The sandbox: cig's kernel does not allow unprivileged user namespaces, so chrome-sandbox is
# setuid root (Chromium's own suid sandbox helper; it only sets up the sandbox and drops root).
